# `reporting/presentations/` — Slide decks

## Authority

See the root [`README.md`](../../README.md), reporting
[`README.md`](../README.md), and [`AGENTS.md`](../AGENTS.md).

Use one artifact folder per talk, conventionally `YYYY-MM-venue/`. Mutable source
may evolve until the talk. A delivered talk is historical: freeze the presented
deck as `deliveries/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<milestone>/`, never edit that delivery, and use
a new folder/delivery for the next talk.

Slides use dark/screen data figures from `results/figures/dark/` and authored
schematics from `assets/figures/`. Beamer decks use their own document class;
they may share `_assets/fonts.tex` and generated theme colors but do not load
`_assets/lab.cls`.

{% if include_example -%}
The optional example deck is `example/slides.tex`. Build the bundled reporting
examples with `make -C reporting slides`.
{% else -%}
This render contains no example deck or reporting Makefile. Create an artifact
folder and use your chosen build command; do not rely on example paths.
{% endif %}

See [`../DELIVERIES.md`](../DELIVERIES.md) for the required immutable manifest
and payload layout.
